  "question": {
    "text": "A point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> moves such that the chord of contact of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> with respect to the circle <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> passes through the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> The coordinates of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> when it is nearest to the origin are"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let, the point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> be <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> then<br />Equation of the chord of contact is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;<br />Since, it passes through <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> so,<br />&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> is the locus of the point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />Hence, the nearest point on <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math>"
  }
